      "translatable": true,
      "contextBefore": "**expressions**: An array of predicate expressions that evaluates to a collection.",
      "contextAfter": "`arguments`: An array containing `NSExpression` objects that will be used as parameters during the invocation of selector. For a selector taking no parameters, the array should be empty. For a selector taking one or more parameters, the array should contain one `NSExpression` object which will evaluate to an instance of the appropriate type for each parameter. If there is a mismatch between the number of parameters expected and the number you provide during evaluation, an exception may be raised or missing parameters may simply be replaced by `nil` (which occurs depends on how many parameters are provided, and whether you have over- or underflow). See [`init(forFunction:arguments:)`](nsexpression/init(forfunction:arguments:).md) for a complete list of arguments.",
